Relevant columns and their possible usage  
actor.actor_id: join key to film_actor  
actor.first_name / actor.last_name: build the actor’s full name to return in the final step  
film_actor.film_id / film_actor.actor_id: bridge table that tells which actor plays in which film  
film.film_id: join key to film_actor / film_category  
film.release_year: filter to 2000‑2010 (inclusive)  
film.language_id: join to language, filter to English  
film.length: running time filter ( ≤ 120 minutes )  
film.rating: filter to ‘G’ or ‘PG’  
language.language_id / language.name: locate English (typically name = 'English')  
film_category.film_id / film_category.category_id: connect films to a category  
category.category_id / category.name: locate ‘Children’ category  

Main conditions you will need  
1. language.name = 'English'  
2. category.name  = 'Children'  
3. film.rating   IN ('G','PG')  
4. film.length  <= 120  
5. film.release_year BETWEEN 2000 AND 2010  

Below are ten exploratory ‑‑> final SQL queries (SQLite dialect).  
Each query is limited to 20 rows so you can inspect results step‑by‑step.  

```sql
-- 1) Description: List all languages so we can confirm the id of English
SELECT DISTINCT name 
FROM language 
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: List all categories to find the id (or just use the name) for Children
SELECT DISTINCT category_id, name 
FROM category 
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: See a sample of all G / PG movies that are ≤120 minutes and were released 2000‑2010
SELECT DISTINCT film_id, title, release_year, rating, length 
FROM film
WHERE rating IN ('G','PG')
  AND length <= 120
  AND release_year BETWEEN 2000 AND 2010
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: Add language = English to the previous film filter
SELECT DISTINCT f.film_id, f.title, f.release_year, f.rating, f.length
FROM film AS f
JOIN language AS l  ON l.language_id = f.language_id
WHERE l.name = 'English'
  AND f.rating IN ('G','PG')
  AND f.length <= 120
  AND f.release_year BETWEEN 2000 AND 2010
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: Bring in category and keep only Children titles
SELECT DISTINCT f.film_id, f.title
FROM film              AS f
JOIN language          AS l  ON l.language_id = f.language_id
JOIN film_category     AS fc ON fc.film_id    = f.film_id
JOIN category          AS c  ON c.category_id = fc.category_id
WHERE l.name = 'English'
  AND c.name = 'Children'
  AND f.rating IN ('G','PG')
  AND f.length <= 120
  AND f.release_year BETWEEN 2000 AND 2010
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: Look at which actor_id values appear in those filtered Children/English/G|PG films
SELECT DISTINCT fa.actor_id
FROM film_actor        AS fa
JOIN film              AS f  ON f.film_id     = fa.film_id
JOIN language          AS l  ON l.language_id = f.language_id
JOIN film_category     AS fc ON fc.film_id    = f.film_id
JOIN category          AS c  ON c.category_id = fc.category_id
WHERE l.name = 'English'
  AND c.name = 'Children'
  AND f.rating IN ('G','PG')
  AND f.length <= 120
  AND f.release_year BETWEEN 2000 AND 2010
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: Convert the list of actor_id to full names (still distinct list, no counting yet)
SELECT DISTINCT a.actor_id,
       a.first_name || ' ' || a.last_name AS full_name
FROM actor             AS a
JOIN film_actor        AS fa ON fa.actor_id  = a.actor_id
JOIN film              AS f  ON f.film_id    = fa.film_id
JOIN language          AS l  ON l.language_id= f.language_id
JOIN film_category     AS fc ON fc.film_id   = f.film_id
JOIN category          AS c  ON c.category_id= fc.category_id
WHERE l.name = 'English'
  AND c.name = 'Children'
  AND f.rating IN ('G','PG')
  AND f.length <= 120
  AND f.release_year BETWEEN 2000 AND 2010
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Description: Count how many times each actor appears in the qualified films
SELECT a.actor_id,
       a.first_name || ' ' || a.last_name AS full_name,
       COUNT(*) AS appearances
FROM actor             AS a
JOIN film_actor        AS fa ON fa.actor_id  = a.actor_id
JOIN film              AS f  ON f.film_id    = fa.film_id
JOIN language          AS l  ON l.language_id= f.language_id
JOIN film_category     AS fc ON fc.film_id   = f.film_id
JOIN category          AS c  ON c.category_id= fc.category_id
WHERE l.name = 'English'
  AND c.name = 'Children'
  AND f.rating IN ('G','PG')
  AND f.length <= 120
  AND f.release_year BETWEEN 2000 AND 2010
GROUP BY a.actor_id, full_name
ORDER BY appearances DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Description: Same as #8 but show only the top actor(s) with the highest count
SELECT a.actor_id,
       a.first_name || ' ' || a.last_name AS full_name,
       COUNT(*) AS appearances
FROM actor             AS a
JOIN film_actor        AS fa ON fa.actor_id  = a.actor_id
JOIN film              AS f  ON f.film_id    = fa.film_id
JOIN language          AS l  ON l.language_id= f.language_id
JOIN film_category     AS fc ON fc.film_id   = f.film_id
JOIN category          AS c  ON c.category_id= fc.category_id
WHERE l.name = 'English'
  AND c.name = 'Children'
  AND f.rating IN ('G','PG')
  AND f.length <= 120
  AND f.release_year BETWEEN 2000 AND 2010
GROUP BY a.actor_id, full_name
ORDER BY appearances DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

```sql
-- 10) Description: Return only the full name of the most‑frequent actor (final answer)
SELECT a.first_name || ' ' || a.last_name AS most_frequent_actor
FROM actor             AS a
JOIN film_actor        AS fa ON fa.actor_id  = a.actor_id
JOIN film              AS f  ON f.film_id    = fa.film_id
JOIN language          AS l  ON l.language_id= f.language_id
JOIN film_category     AS fc ON fc.film_id   = f.film_id
JOIN category          AS c  ON c.category_id= fc.category_id
WHERE l.name = 'English'
  AND c.name = 'Children'
  AND f.rating IN ('G','PG')
  AND f.length <= 120
  AND f.release_year BETWEEN 2000 AND 2010
GROUP BY a.actor_id, most_frequent_actor
ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

